 "161": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Self-test every assessment in both directions \u2014 how likely a student could score well without demonstrating the understanding sought (by guessing, parroting, effort, lovely products, or articulateness), and how likely a student could score poorly despite significant understanding (because the task is irrelevant or the criteria arbitrary) \u2014 and treat anything other than very unlikely on either as meaning the evidence is probably not valid."
 },
 "162": {
  "action": "split"
 },
 "163": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Address the two distinct reliability problems in performance assessment separately \u2014 generalizing from too few performances (a result may reflect an untypical day rather than a pattern) and judges scoring the same performance differently \u2014 using multiple tasks for the same outcome and well-trained supervised judges working from clear rubrics and specific anchors, accepting that measurement error is unavoidable and can only be minimized to tolerable levels."
 },
