 "454": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Estimate teaching load with the 20 Percent Rule \u2014 an ordinary three-credit course taught well takes about 20 percent of a term (three contact hours plus about six hours of preparation and grading against a forty-five-hour week), adjusted up for high enrolment or frequent writing and down for a graduate assistant or fewer credits, with separate allowance for supervision and advising \u2014 and double the estimate for a course taught for the first time, since new preparations are almost always overlooked."
 },
 "455": {
  "action": "confirm",
  "canonical": "Set faculty-work expectations jointly and up front rather than leaving the trade-offs to the individual \u2014 the faculty member lists intended activities, the chair or committee weighs them against departmental needs, adjustments are negotiated with all parties present \u2014 and make the revisable agreement the basis for a year-end assessment that fosters growth of both the individual and the institution."
 },
